# spark-vm credential store: ntindle may touch swapd's secrets ONLY through
# these narrow, name-validated wrapper scripts. No shell access — a sudoers
# `*` in a path component matches `/`, so literal paths are used for every
# command below. Exactly one argument wildcard exists in this file (the
# whois peer IP, documented at the rule); argument wildcards cannot match
# `/` their way into a different command the way path wildcards can, and
# that one is read-only — see the rule's comment.
ntindle ALL=(swapd) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/bin/cred-store-set
ntindle ALL=(swapd) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/bin/cred-store-set-inference
# inference proxy (Security review, PR #126 reconcile): blind compare
# for the gate fixture installer's fail-closed guard. Reads the
# candidate from stdin, exits 0/1/2, and NEVER prints the stored value;
# the installer compares against its own public dummy, so the one leaked
# bit reveals nothing about a real credential. No wildcard needed (the
# path is the inference proxy's single fixed credential name, the
# candidate travels on stdin), and the file's one-wildcard invariant
# stays intact.
ntindle ALL=(swapd) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/bin/cred-store-verify-inference
ntindle ALL=(swapd) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/bin/cred-store-get
ntindle ALL=(swapd) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/bin/cred-store-delete
ntindle ALL=(swapd) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/bin/cred-registry-set
ntindle ALL=(swapd) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/bin/cred-registry-set-inference
ntindle ALL=(swapd) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/cat /home/swapd/credentials.json
ntindle ALL=(swapd) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/cat /home/swapd/inference-registry.json
ntindle ALL=(swapd) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/ls /home/swapd/secrets
# inference proxy (finding 31): append-only hosts file, listable secrets dir
ntindle ALL=(swapd) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/tee -a /home/swapd/inference-hosts.allow
ntindle ALL=(swapd) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/ls /home/swapd/inference-secrets
# inference proxy (findings 29, 31): the gate fixture's loopback SSRF
# exemption lives in the inference instance's OWN ssrf file, never the
# main proxy's shared one -- the main proxy's egress guard is untouched.
# The install-gate-fixture fail-closed guard lists the secrets dir above.
ntindle ALL=(swapd) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/tee -a /home/swapd/inference-ssrf.allow
# confirmd (finding 47, 63b): narrow tailscale rules for the self-peer
# check. whois takes a peer IP; ip takes no args.
# The whois rule carries the file's one intentional argument wildcard:
# the peer IP varies per request, so it cannot be a literal. This is
# safe because whois is a read-only single-peer lookup with no mutating
# flags, and confirmd passes the peer IP as one argv element (no shell).
# Do not extend the wildcard to any other tailscale subcommand.
swapd ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/tailscale whois --json *
swapd ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/tailscale ip
swapd ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/tailscale ip -4
swapd ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/tailscale status --json
